  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gollob&#xe9;, le Mirroir de la femme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">It is a project that aims at the empowerment and the valorization of women. The project will be implemented by the association of Young Girls Leaders Gollobe of Torodi over a period of 12 months; the town of Torodi and 03 villages of the said town will be targeted in partnership with the local authorities and technical services of Torodi; for a total of 400 direct beneficiaries. Five main activities will be implemented:
Advocacy at the communal level to promote access to land for young girls and women
Encouraging the schooling of young girls by accompanying them through sensitizations
Court hearings to allow 100 women with disabilities to obtain birthcertificates
Capacity building for these women to participate in income generating activities
Sensitization of women leaders to fight and denounce all forms of violence
The project encourages the participation of women in development actions, the empowerment of young girls and women with disabilities. Indeed, women are often marginalized in rural areas. The actions of the girl leaders will give a voice to women who are discriminated against in terms of land management and sharing. The women leaders of the department will be put in contributions to launch an advocacy at the level of the communal authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">## Gollob&#xe9; ## is an association of young girls leaders in the department of Torodi. The association was created in March 2018 thanks to the initiative of the NGO Dev circle in order to develop a community approach of participation of the girl in the development of their community by developing their leadership.
We had organized several awareness-raising activities for young people on issues of peace, drug use and citizenship.
On the sidelines of the 2019/2020 return to school We had organized several caravans on the education of the girl, the retention of the girl in school, forced marriage and lawsuits which are the reasons put forward by many parents to end to their children&apos;s education.
As citizen action, we held several sanitation sessions in the town hall, the prefecture, thehealth center. We also organized health campaigns, the latest of which was echoed and supported by local authorities. This is the zero plastic campaign in the city of Torodi. An initiative that mobilized a large part of the population and especially the association of young people who were not interested in protecting the environment.
The association is involved in several activities and workshops in the department of Torodi.
We had to mobilize the authorities, the decision-makers and the actors of the civil society in our activities and this made it possible to promote several keys of Torodi.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jeunes filles leaders de Torodi ##G</narrative>
  </participating-org>
